!/native/Cargo.lock
native/target/
# The sandbox runner is native code built per platform by
# `scripts/build_native_runner.py` and by the release workflow. The directory
# and its `__init__.py` are tracked; the binaries never are.
raiker/native/*/
output/
# Playwright writes its last-run marker beside the config unless outputDir
# covers it; the evidence itself lives in output/ and docs/plans/screenshots.
test-results/
# The two round-stamped capture folders were removed from the repository on
# 2026-09-06 (roughly a hundred megabytes of binaries). Sixty-three live specs
# still write into them, and `page.screenshot` creates the parent directory, so
# a live round recreates both — as *untracked* files that a `git add -A` would
# happily commit straight back in. The captures are still worth taking and
# looking at; they are not worth carrying in the tree.
docs/plans/screenshots/working/
docs/plans/screenshots/not-working/
# Working captures taken while driving the app during development. Four of
# these reached a commit before this line existed, which is the same hundred
# megabytes of binaries arriving one convenience at a time.
/*.png
